                            filter-fn
                            candidates-fn
                            create-fn
                            require-match
                            (expand-aliases t))
  "Select and find a note.

If OTHER-WINDOW, visit the NOTE in another window.

CANDIDATES-FN is the function to query candidates for selection,
which takes as its argument a filtering function (see FILTER-FN).
Unless specified, `cyberdeck-find-default-candidates-source' is
used.

FILTER-FN is the function to apply on the candidates, which takes
as its argument a `cyberdeck-aiu'. Unless specified,
`cyberdeck-find-default-filter' is used.

CREATE-FN controls how a new note is created when user selects a
non-existent note (only possible when REQUIRE-MATCH is nil). Like
the CREATE-FN of `cyberdeck-insert', it is called with two arguments
- the typed title and capture unfoldings (currently always nil).
It should return the created `cyberdeck-aiu' to visit, or nil to
skip visiting. Unless specified, `cyberdeck-find-default-create-fn'
is used.

When REQUIRE-MATCH is nil user may select a non-existent note,
which is then created via CREATE-FN. When non-nil, only existing
notes may be selected.

When EXPAND-ALIASES is non-nil (the default), each note with
aliases will appear multiple times in the completion list - once
for the original title and once for each alias."
  (interactive)
  (let* ((region-text
          (when (region-active-p)
            (org-link-display-format
             (buffer-substring-no-properties
              (set-marker
               (make-marker) (region-beginning))
              (set-marker
               (make-marker) (region-end))))))
         (note (cyberdeck-select-from
                "AIU"
                (funcall
                 (or
                  candidates-fn
                  cyberdeck-find-default-candidates-source)
                 (or
                  filter-fn
                  cyberdeck-find-default-filter))
                :require-match require-match
                :initial-prompt region-text
                :expand-aliases expand-aliases)))
    (if (cyberdeck-aiu-id note)
        ;; Existing AIU - visit it
        (cyberdeck-visit note other-window)
      ;; New AIU - create it
      (when (not require-match)
        (let ((new-aiu (funcall (or create-fn
                                     cyberdeck-find-default-create-fn)
                                 (cyberdeck-aiu-title note)
                                 nil)))
          (when new-aiu
            (let ((new-path (cyberdeck-aiu-path new-aiu))
                  (cur-path (or (buffer-file-name)
                                (when (fboundp 'org-capture-get)
                                  (let ((b (ignore-errors (org-capture-get :buffer))))
                                    (when (bufferp b) (buffer-file-name b)))))))
              ;; Never steal the buffer while our own "n" capture is still
