** Birth enrollment (Installation Protocol fundamental)
Every AIU is born into the review pool — learn it all or
deliberately suspend it, no third state. The single seam is the
public `cyberdeck-create' above (both file and heading
branches funnel through it), so specialized creators (recipes,
dictionary, AIU Runs, journal, aiu-context-aius) need no individual
wiring. AIUs under =admin/= (aiu-context-aius, Journal, admin
queues) are metadata or logs, not knowledge cards, and are excluded
by path — reviewing them would pollute sessions with machinery.
Anything enrolled later by hand (mark-review, attest, encounter)
uses the same init path, so enrollment is idempotent by
construction: existing stages are never downgraded here, only
missing ones are set.

Load-order note: files compile in AIU Subnet order, so every call below is guarded
by `fboundp'. At creation time in a live session everything is
loaded; the guards only protect batch/headless partial loads.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(defun my/cyberdeck--admin-path-p (file)
  "Non-nil when FILE lives under the vault's admin/ territory.
Covers admin/unfoldings/, admin/Journal/, and admin queues alike."
  (when file
    (string-prefix-p
     (expand-file-name "admin/" (my/cyberdeck-root-dir))
     (file-truename file))))

(defun my/cyberdeck--enroll-new-aiu (note)
  "Enroll NOTE in mastering at birth: STAGE=AWARE, STATUS=ACTIVE.
Skips admin/ paths. Never downgrades an existing stage (transplants
may arrive with one); only fills in what is missing, ensures the
schedule row exists, and syncs the first tag. Returns AIU."
  (when (and note
             (fboundp 'my/cyberdeck-installation-protocol--init-schedule)
             (fboundp 'my/cyberdeck-installation-protocol--sync-stage-tag))
    (let ((file (cyberdeck-aiu-path note)))
      (when (and file (file-exists-p file)
                 (not (my/cyberdeck--admin-path-p file)))
        (let ((stage nil) (status nil))
          (with-current-buffer (find-file-noselect file)
            (save-excursion
              (let ((level (cyberdeck-aiu-level note))
                    (pos (cyberdeck-aiu-pos note)))
                (if (and level (> level 0) pos)
                    (progn (goto-char pos) (org-back-to-heading t))
                  (goto-char (point-min)))
                (setq stage (my/cyberdeck--drawer-get "STAGE"))
                (setq status (my/cyberdeck--drawer-get "STATUS")))))
          ;; Birth rule: human creation is the awareness gate. Anything
          ;; already at ACQUIRING or above (transplants) is left alone.
          (let ((idx (if (and stage (fboundp 'my/cyberdeck-installation-protocol--stage-index))
                         (my/cyberdeck-installation-protocol--stage-index stage)
                       -1)))
            (when (< idx 1)
              (my/cyberdeck-installation-protocol--put note "STAGE" "AWARE")
              (setq stage "AWARE")))
          (unless status
            (my/cyberdeck-installation-protocol--put note "STATUS" "ACTIVE"))
          (my/cyberdeck-installation-protocol--init-schedule nil note)
          (my/cyberdeck-installation-protocol--sync-stage-tag note (or stage "AWARE"))))))
  note)
