*** Installation
#+begin_src emacs-lisp :tangle no
;; Functions load via org evaluation; the tangled artifact lives at
;; infra/elisp/capture.el (tangle target of this file).
#+end_src

Turns plain org outlines into registered prompts. A declarative file has
a level-1 heading shaped like a PROPERTY_KEY with plain org tags for
kind and contexts, whose level-2 headings are the allowed options —
no elisp. Editing headings edits the prompt; adding a file adds an
AIU Context; deleting a file removes it. Files that contain src blocks
are treated as legacy elisp prompts and skipped.

Tag vocabulary on the level-1 heading, e.g. ~* MY_KEY :unfolding:file:heading:~:
KIND (first match wins): AIU Context|inline|todo|multi|tags|tagopt|template|free|scoped|Installation Protocol|AIU Subnet|body   (default: AIU Context)
CONTEXTS (all matches, space-joined): file|heading|task|AIU Run|dictionary|contact|recipe|rule   (default: file heading)
Unknown tags are ignored. No #+ file keywords; no :LABEL: (KEY is the label).
A :PROPERTIES: drawer holding only :ID: may follow the heading.

