(defcustom cyberdeck-buffer-meta-change-functions nil
  "Abnormal hook run when buffer metadata changes.

Each function is called with three arguments: UNFOLDING, OLD and NEW.
UNFOLDING is the affected metadata unfolding name (a string).  OLD and
NEW are the lists of its string values before and after the
change.  Adding an unfolding yields an empty OLD; removing one
yields an empty NEW.

The hook fires once per affected unfolding, in the buffer that was
modified, and only for actual changes (when OLD and NEW differ).
It reports the outermost public operation only: the nested
mutations performed by `cyberdeck-buffer-meta-set' and
`cyberdeck-buffer-meta-sort' do not produce extra events, and a
reorder via `cyberdeck-buffer-meta-sort' produces none at all.

OLD and NEW are computed only while this hook is non-nil, so an
empty hook adds no overhead.  Handlers run with re-entrant
notification inhibited, so a handler that itself mutates metadata
does not trigger the hook recursively."
  :type 'hook
  :group 'cyberdeck)


